=== Complete Solutions

#sol-item(1, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[NCDs are generally not transmitted directly between people as infections are. Malaria is an infection, whereas diabetes is not spread directly like an infection.]

#sol-item(2, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Diabetes is a noncommunicable condition. A category is useful for study but is not an individual diagnosis.]

#sol-item(3, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Cardiovascular diseases are a major NCD category. The heart and blood vessels form the cardiovascular system.]

#sol-item(4, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Chronic respiratory diseases affect breathing and lung function. Clinical assessment is needed when symptoms are concerning.]

#sol-item(5, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Cancers are a group of diseases involving abnormal cell growth. Different cancers have different causes and treatments.]

#sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Diabetes involves problems regulating blood glucose; types and management differ. Individual diagnosis and treatment require qualified assessment.]

#sol-item(7, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Cardiovascular diseases involve the heart and blood vessels. Care and prevention depend on the person and condition.]

#sol-item(8, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[NCDs arise from interacting factors that vary by condition and person. Risk is shaped by multiple interacting influences.]

#sol-item(9, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Some infectious agents increase the risk of certain cancers without making all cancers contagious. The infection and the resulting cancer risk are distinct concepts.]

#sol-item(10, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Risk describes probability, not certainty or a complete diagnosis. A risk factor does not establish an individual diagnosis.]

#sol-item(11, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Many factors can contribute to disease risk.]

#sol-item(12, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Tobacco exposure increases risk of several diseases, though outcomes vary.]

#sol-item(13, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Air pollution can contribute to respiratory and cardiovascular disease.]

#sol-item(14, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Alcohol use can increase risks of injury and several diseases.]

#sol-item(15, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Dietary patterns and activity can contribute to risk alongside other factors.]

#sol-item(16, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Some factors can be modified, though opportunities differ between people.]

#sol-item(17, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Age and inherited characteristics are not readily modified and do not alone establish diagnosis.]

#sol-item(18, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Resources and environments influence whether preventive actions are feasible.]

#sol-item(19, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Education, access and supportive environments can work together.]

#sol-item(20, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Screening depends on current guidance, age, risk and circumstances.]

#sol-item(21, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Do not change prescribed care without appropriate individual advice.]

#sol-item(22, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Mental health is part of overall health and interacts with other dimensions.]

#sol-item(23, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A diagnosis requires appropriate assessment, not a single experience.]

#sol-item(24, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Ongoing distress or difficulty functioning may warrant professional assessment.]

#sol-item(25, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Mental health conditions are health concerns, not moral failures.]

#sol-item(26, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Listening and helping the person access support can be useful.]

#sol-item(27, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Supportive practices can help wellbeing but may not substitute for treatment.]

#sol-item(28, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Immediate danger calls for urgent help; stay with the person when safe and involve appropriate services.]

#sol-item(29, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Immediate safety can require involving emergency or safeguarding services.]

#sol-item(30, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Stigma can create barriers to support and care.]

#sol-item(31, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Severe chest pain can be an emergency and requires prompt assessment.]

#sol-item(32, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Sudden neurological symptoms can be signs of an emergency.]

#sol-item(33, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Concerning symptoms can have serious causes and require timely help.]

#sol-item(34, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Educational material is not a substitute for professional assessment.]

#sol-item(35, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Appearance and size alone do not establish a complete diagnosis.]

#sol-item(36, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Risk reduction is probabilistic and cannot guarantee an outcome.]

#sol-item(37, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Privacy matters, but immediate safety and safeguarding can require appropriate action.]

#sol-item(38, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Management depends on diagnosis, circumstances and professional assessment.]

#sol-item(39, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Community conditions and access influence prevention and care.]

#sol-item(40, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Some infections increase certain cancer risks without making all cancers contagious.]
